{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Just as they were appalled at you.</b> Like ושממו עליה אויביכם (Leviticus 26:32). The meaning: everyone who sees the servant of HaShem will be appalled." "And the meaning of <b>many</b>: the nations." "And the meaning of <b>so</b>: as if he said 'so it was.' כן משחת מאיש — and behold, משחת תאר of HaShem." "<b>And his form.</b> It comes by way of רחבו, and this is well known, for there are many nations in the world who think that the form of the Jew is different from all forms, and they ask whether a Jew has a mouth or an eye — so [I have heard] in the land of Ishmael and in Edom."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 52, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:17.120594379Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}